# The SDD workspace is scratch: ledgers, briefs, reports and review packages are
# per-session working files and stay out of the repository.
*
# ...with one exception. global-constraints.md stopped being scratch hours into the
# first session that used it: every dispatch cites it as binding, several lanes write
# to it, and an untracked file has no index, no diff, no history and no protection
# against a concurrent overwrite -- so none of the three shared-file rules it itself
# states can apply to it. Tracking it turns that whole class of hazard back into the
# one the rulebook already covers. `!*/` lets git descend; `*` still ignores the rest.
!*/
!.gitignore
!global-constraints.md
